<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- RoseyBot Robot Description File

     Generated from the SolidWorks to URDF exporter (URDF_FIN export); every
     link, joint, and mass property comes from that export, except:
       - base_footprint is the root (REP-105), on the ground plane below
         base_link; the export had it as a child of base_link.
       - base_footprint, imu_link, and camera_*_optical_link are virtual
         frames with no mass, inertia, or geometry.
       - All wheel joints rotate about +y, so a positive velocity drives the
         robot forward on both sides (the export used -y on the left wheels).
       - Mesh paths point at this package; meshes are decimated copies.
       - base_link.STL was exported in the wrong frame (offset by the
         mocap_mast_joint origin), so its visual/collision origin shifts it
         back into base_link. -->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
